## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 (.NET 10) | **File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`
**Integration calibration applied:** Class has `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 0           | 0              |
| Low      | 1           | 1              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)
**Rationale:** Even in integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` introduces non-determinism and slows the suite by a fixed 3 seconds.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — poll with timeout
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures on slow CI; 3 s added to every run unconditionally.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)
**Rationale:** The `if/else` means only one branch ever executes per run — you don't know which behavior was verified.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — split into two deterministic tests
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName() { ... }

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount() { ... }
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden test gap — one path is never exercised, giving false confidence.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)
**Rationale:** No assertion; passes even if every insert silently fails. Name implies "does not throw" intent but the framework already catches unhandled exceptions.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — verify observable outcome
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

Assert.AreEqual(100, _repository.ListAll().Count);
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False-pass — test reports green while data is silently discarded.

---

#### 🟡 LOW — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)
**Rationale:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. On failure, the MSTest runner shows the assert that failed but not *why* the expected value was chosen.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

```csharp
// ✅ Fix — add diagnostic messages
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id must be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower failure diagnosis in CI logs (minor for 4 assertions, worse as count grows).

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused scope |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, single assertion, deterministic |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion (`3`) is self-documenting (3 items just added) — no Magic Number smell |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async, clear assertion, legitimate integration pattern |

The use of an **in-memory SQLite connection** avoids Mystery Guest — the database is hermetic and requires no external state. General Fixture is also clean: both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | ~1 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 focused tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop | ~10 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to assertions | ~2 min |

Fix #1 first — it's the highest risk (silent false-passes) with the lowest effort.
